From: FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket port
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: preserve RPPocket power-on sequence

The RPPocket stock USB2PHY driver clears phy_sus and waits for UTMI clock
stability without resetting the PHY afterward. Mainline performs an additional
reset that prevents the board's internal RTL8188EUS from reconnecting when DWC2
is loaded after resume.

Skip only that extra reset on the RPPocket. The stock-matched sequence has been
validated across cold boot and repeated suspend/resume reload cycles.

---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -628,7 +628,10 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	 * please keep the common_on_n 1'b0 to set these blocks
 	 * remain powered.
 	 */
-	ret = rockchip_usb2phy_reset(rphy);
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("funnyplaying,rppocket"))
+		ret = 0;
+	else
+		ret = rockchip_usb2phy_reset(rphy);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
